  "summary": "# Health-Tech News Digest — September 23, 2026\n\nBehavioral health platforms are consolidating care delivery with AI-powered triage, as Pelago and Array Behavioral Care both launched new systems to streamline patient assessment and treatment connections across substance use, mental health, and behavioral addiction services. Meanwhile, AI adoption is accelerating across clinical settings—Intermountain Health reported a 22-percentage-point jump in chart completion rates with AI documentation tools, Oracle Health embedded its nurse AI agent directly into EHR workflows to reduce context switching, and Epic's mortality prediction algorithm is advancing geriatric care capabilities, though healthcare leaders are calling for a \"probation period\" to establish shared playbooks for safely onboarding autonomous AI agents beyond pilots.\n\nSignificant M&A and funding activity reflects investor confidence in specialized therapeutics and health platforms. Telix is acquiring radiopharmaceutical developer ITM for $1.65 billion, while Electra Therapeutics raised $350 million in an upsized IPO for precision immunology drugs, and Heidi Health reached a $900 million valuation on $340 million in funding. On the policy side, HHS announced new initiatives to reduce animal testing in drug development, CMS is expanding its outcomes-based ACCESS model to heart failure, COPD, and substance use disorders starting spring 2027, and RFK Jr. has overhauled the USPSTF leadership with eight new appointments, signaling potential shifts in preventive care priorities.",
